1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,430
This is Watch Me.

2
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:05,259
It listens only when you ask it to, and it only answers to your voice.

3
00:00:06,599 --> 00:00:11,647
In a recent lawsuit, a student said she felt like bait at a fraternity party, and that she had been drugged.

4
00:00:11,647 --> 00:00:12,629
The case is disputed.

5
00:00:12,629 --> 00:00:15,059
Someone who's been drugged can't say they're not OK.

6
00:00:16,759 --> 00:00:20,804
And at home, more than one in three women has faced violence from a partner.

7
00:00:20,804 --> 00:00:23,093
Nearly half of it never reaches the police.

8
00:00:23,093 --> 00:00:26,179
When reaching for a phone isn't safe, her voice is enough.

9
00:00:27,779 --> 00:00:29,239
First, she says one line.

10
00:00:29,239 --> 00:00:33,443
Watch Me turns her voice into a voiceprint, drawn here as a fingerprint.

11
00:00:33,443 --> 00:00:37,879
From now on, only this voice can start Watch Me, stop it, or answer, I'm OK.

12
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,719
At a party, she says: watch me.

13
00:01:03,379 --> 00:01:06,179
Muse Spark reads what it hears, and decides to ask.

14
00:01:09,779 --> 00:01:11,370
She's too dizzy to answer.

15
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:17,180
So Watch Me texts and calls the people she chose, with what it heard and a map of where she is.

16
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:18,219
Here, in dry run.

17
00:01:28,979 --> 00:01:31,907
Now someone grabs her phone and says, stop watching.

18
00:01:31,907 --> 00:01:32,977
It isn't her voice.

19
00:01:32,977 --> 00:01:36,299
Watch Me refuses, keeps recording, and asks her right away.

20
00:01:38,679 --> 00:01:40,511
Not all harassment is an emergency.

21
00:01:40,511 --> 00:01:42,866
At office hours, she switches to Notice mode.

22
00:01:42,866 --> 00:01:44,280
Nothing will interrupt her.

23
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:16,352
When she stops, Muse Wonder shows which exact words match how the EEOC describes harassment.

24
00:02:16,352 --> 00:02:17,278
Strings attached.

25
00:02:17,278 --> 00:02:18,258
Getting her alone.

26
00:02:18,258 --> 00:02:19,620
It never decides for her.

27
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,797
And it counts patterns.

28
00:02:20,797 --> 00:02:25,800
This is the third time from the same professor, kept in a dated record that shows if anyone changes it.

29
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:29,781
Under the hood: Whisper and a voiceprint on the device.

30
00:02:29,781 --> 00:02:34,856
Muse Voice Transcribe hears the last minute again, and Muse Spark analyses it and decides.

31
00:02:34,856 --> 00:02:35,984
Muse Wonder reviews.

32
00:02:35,984 --> 00:02:41,623
On 22 realistic scenes, it asked in nine of eleven harmful ones, with no needless check-ins.

33
00:02:41,623 --> 00:02:44,499
Given a perfect transcript, Muse caught all eleven.

34
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:46,692
Watch Me.

35
00:02:46,692 --> 00:02:47,513
You turn it on.

36
00:02:47,513 --> 00:02:49,099
Only your voice turns it off.

37
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:50,960
And only you decide what happened.

